{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Go as the implementation language since Hyperledger Fabric is primarily written in Go and the existing API conventions (protos, bccsp) are Go-based.",
    "For U1, modify the read set proto to include the actual value (and current version) alongside the key/version, preserving backward compatibility by treating the new field as optional; legacy peers can continue to operate against old-format read sets.",
    "For U1, perform the cross-peer value comparison in the VSCC (validation system chaincode) by inspecting the read/write sets of every endorsing peer's transaction proposal response, discarding the transaction if any peer's read set value for the same key/version differs.",
    "For U2-U8, create a new standalone Go package (e.g., internal/pkg/configtx) that does NOT import the fabric/common/genesisconfig or viper packages; instead copy and adapt the necessary structures (Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Consortiums, Capabilities, Policies, Organization, etc.) directly into the new package.",
    "Use a functional-options pattern for the new configuration library (as shown in the U2 snippet) so the API is extensible and decoupled from viper/yaml.",
    "Use the existing bccsp interface for any signing/verification needs (U3, U4); callers supply the key material, and the library does not assume an MSP folder layout or perform I/O to disk.",
    "For U7, implement diff computation by walking the config groups recursively (using protolator-style protojson/JSON encoding) so that only fields that differ between base and modified become entries in the resulting ConfigUpdate; this mirrors the behavior of `configtxlator compute_update`.",
    "For U8, operate on the system channel (orderer system group) configuration and add the org definition under the named consortium by mutating the Consortiums map and serializing the resulting ConfigGroup; the output is a ConfigUpdate envelope, not a signed transaction.",
    "Adopt a shared internal helper layer (proto marshal/unmarshal, ConfigGroup walk/lookup, signature aggregation utilities) used by U2-U8 to avoid duplication.",
    "Provide unit tests for every new function using golden-file proto comparisons (`proto.Equal`) against known-good outputs produced by `configtxgen`, `cryptogen`, `configtxlator`, and `protolator`.",
    "Keep U1 changes opt-in via a feature flag / chaincode-level configuration so existing networks are not broken, and clearly document the upgrade/migration story for endorsement policy and read set version."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced developer with prior Hyperledger Fabric codebase knowledge is implementing all of this work.",
    "The implementation targets Hyperledger Fabric 2.x APIs and proto definitions.",
    "Reference outputs (golden protos) used for comparison in U2, U5, U6, U7, U8 can be generated by running the existing `configtxgen`, `cryptogen`, `configtxlator`, and `protolator` tools on a representative `configtx.yaml` and MSP directory; these references are available or reproducible.",
    "The U1 work includes proto schema changes and therefore requires regenerated Go proto stubs; this regeneration is mechanical and counted inside the implementation effort.",
    "Backward compatibility for U1 means: if some endorsing peers still produce read sets without values, the validating peer falls back to the current key/version-only behavior rather than rejecting the transaction; this is implemented as a defensive default.",
    "No new third-party dependencies are introduced beyond what Fabric already uses (bccsp, fabric-protos, golang/protobuf, etc.).",
    "The 'fit-for-purpose library' is delivered as an internal Go package within the existing Fabric repository (similar to the historical `fabric-config` work), not a separate module.",
    "Testing effort covers unit tests and small integration tests; it does not include a full end-to-end Fabric network bring-up with orderer/peers/CLI for every story.",
    "Documentation effort covers GoDoc comments and a short README for the new package; it does not include external release notes or tutorials.",
    "The detached signature format produced in U3 and consumed in U4 is the same SHA256-based signature over the ConfigUpdate bytes that the existing `signtx` peer command produces, so the acceptance test in U4 (equivalence with `signtx`) can be checked mechanically.",
    "Estimates assume uninterrupted focus on the increment with no significant rework caused by upstream Fabric changes mid-development."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project setup, shared infrastructure, and adapted types",
      "activity_description": "Create the new Go package, set up its module/path, copy and adapt the relevant structures from fabric/common/genesisconfig (Profile, Application, Orderer, Consortium, Consortiums, Capabilities, Policies, Organization, etc.) into the new package, and implement shared internal helpers (proto marshal/unmarshal, ConfigGroup walk/lookup, options pattern).",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Analysis and design of read set with values",
      "activity_description": "Study the current endorsement/commit flow, the KvRead proto, VSCC validation logic, and the behavior described in the referenced Medium article. Produce a short design describing the proto change, the validation rule, backward-compatibility semantics, and the upgrade path.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Proto schema and endorsement-side changes",
      "activity_description": "Add a value field (and ensure version is preserved) to the read set proto, regenerate Go proto stubs, and update the endorser/chaincode shim so the actual value read from the world state is included in the read set of the proposal response alongside the key and version.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Validator-side (VSCC) value comparison",
      "activity_description": "Update the validation system chaincode (VSCC) so that, after the standard endorsement-policy check, it compares the read sets across endorsing peers' proposal responses key-by-key (and version-by-version); if any peer reports a different value for the same key/version, the transaction is marked invalid with an appropriate TxValidationCode. Implement graceful fallback when values are absent.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Unit and integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests covering: (a) tampered single-peer world state, (b) all peers consistent, (c) mix of old-format and new-format read sets, (d) endorsement policy violations still rejected, (e) happy-path commits unaffected. Add a small integration test that exercises the scenario from the referenced article.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - CreateChannelTx function implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement CreateChannelTx(ChannelConfig, ...Option) (*cb.Block, error) that builds an orderer genesis block from the provided Profile/Application/Orderer/Consortium/Consortiums/Capabilities/Policies structures (loaded from caller-supplied data, not viper/yaml), producing a proto-encoded block that is `proto.Equal` to the output of `configtxgen -channelID ... -profile ...` on a prototypical configtx.yaml.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that load a representative configtx.yaml and MSP folder via the existing tools, generate a reference genesis block with configtxgen, and assert `proto.Equal` against the output of CreateChannelTx for several channel profiles.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Detached signature on ChannelUpdate",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes a ConfigUpdate (Envelope or ConfigUpdateEnvelope) and caller-supplied key material (via bccsp key or sign interface) and returns a detached signature bytes that can later be combined with other signatures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that sign a sample ConfigUpdate using the new function and verify the signature verifies against the corresponding public key and matches the signature the existing `signtx` command would produce over the same bytes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Assemble signed ConfigUpdate from detached signatures",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes a ConfigUpdate and a collection of detached signatures (each with the signing identity) and produces a fully signed, orderer- and peer-validatable channel config update transaction. The output must be equivalent to that produced by iteratively applying `signtx` to gather n required signatures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that build a config update with multiple detached signatures through the new function and through a sequence of `signtx` invocations, and assert `proto.Equal` on the resulting signed envelopes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Channel update transaction for max_message_count",
      "activity_description": "Implement a fit-for-purpose function that, given the current channel config and a new max_message_count batch size value, returns an unsigned ConfigUpdate that changes only the BatchSize.MaxMessageCount field. The output must match (ignoring any signature) a config update produced manually with configtxlator/protolator.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that generate a reference unsigned config update via the existing tools and assert `proto.Equal` against the new function's output, plus a negative test that confirms no other fields are modified.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U6 - ConfigGroup for an Organization",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes the necessary cryptographic material (root CA/intermediate CA certs, TLS CA certs, MSP ID, OU classifications, admin/peer/orderer/node OU identifiers, etc.) directly as parameters (not from an on-disk MSP folder) and returns a ConfigGroup proto semantically equivalent to that produced by `cryptogen` and `configtxgen -printOrg`.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that run cryptogen + configtxgen -printOrg on a representative MSP folder to obtain a reference ConfigGroup, call the new function with the same crypto material passed in explicitly, and assert semantic equivalence (proto.Equal after normalizing formatting where appropriate).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Compute ConfigUpdate from base and modified configs",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that, given two config transactions (base and modified), computes the ConfigUpdate message that would transform base into modified. The function should require nothing beyond the two transactions. Output must be semantically equivalent to `configtxlator compute_update`.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that run the manual `configtxlator proto_encode --type=common.Config` / `compute_update` / `proto_decode` flow on several sample base/modified pairs and assert the new function's ConfigUpdate matches the reference (modulo signature fields and well-known ID formatting).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Add org definition to a named consortium",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes the current system channel config, a consortium name, and a new organization definition (crypto material as in U6) and returns an unsigned config update transaction that adds the org to the named consortium within the system channel configuration. Output must match (modulo signatures) the result of the documented manual flow with configtxgen -printOrg, protolator, and configtxgen. Channel creation itself is out of scope.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests that reproduce the documented manual procedure to add an org to a consortium and assert `proto.Equal` (ignoring signatures) against the new function's output, including a case for an unknown consortium and an already-present org.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Cross-story integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Integration tests that compose the new functions end-to-end: create a channel (U2), compute a config update adding an org to a consortium (U8) over the resulting config, sign it (U3) with multiple collected signatures (U4), compute an update diff for max_message_count (U5/U7), and verify the resulting transactions validate against Fabric's orderer/peer validation rules on a small in-memory harness.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Documentation",
      "activity_description": "GoDoc comments on every exported function, a package-level README describing the library's purpose and usage patterns, and brief migration notes for U1 (read set with values) covering proto change, feature flag, and upgrade behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 304
  }
}
